WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:13.000
These are the incompressible Navier-Stokes equations. They describe a fluid's velocity u, pressure p, viscosity, and an external force f. The second equation says the flow does not compress.

00:13.400 --> 00:23.127
Some things are proved. In nineteen thirty four, Leray showed that weak solutions exist for all time. In two dimensions, smooth solutions last for ever.

00:23.527 --> 00:30.554
In three dimensions, smooth solutions exist for a short time. They last for ever if the starting flow is small enough.

00:30.954 --> 00:46.133
In September twenty twenty six, the Clay Mathematics Institute acknowledged an announced apparent resolution of the three-dimensional problem. Its evaluation process continues. The problem page remains marked Active as of October twenty ninth.

00:46.533 --> 00:54.324
These exercises check deductions from stated assumptions. They do not verify any proposed solution of the fluid equations.
